{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228817-dreaming-uratha","id":228817,"title":"Dreaming Uratha","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-14T22:54:56-07:00","id":228817,"title":"Dreaming Uratha","content":"I read now <b>Astral Realms</b> for <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>, and there is very interesting sidebar:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Uratha (see <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b>) often roam the Dreaming Earth. To them, doing so is no stranger than a human exploring his own dreamscape. In fact, the practice is so unexceptional that werewolves don\u2019t think of their travels as much more <br /> than a holy dream. </div> </div> </div>My <b>Werewolf</b>-fu isn't high, but I couldn't remeber any thing about &quot;holy dreams&quot;. Dreaming Earth is dream-soul realm of whole planet. It is said that it could be a living conciseness of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaia_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Gaea</b></a>, that should be Incarnea of Earth, like Luna is for the Moon.<br /> <br /> So what are your thoughts on topic? Is there a special dreams for Uratha? Were they come? Is it really from Gaea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T00:33:58-07:00","id":228858,"title":"","content":"&quot;My <b>Werewolf</b>-fu isn't high, but I couldn't remeber any thing about &quot;holy dreams&quot;. &quot;<br /> <br /> The Cahalith auspice ability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T01:46:22-07:00","id":228895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228817-dreaming-uratha?p=228858#post228858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cahalith auspice ability?</div> </div> </div> </div>With journeys to lands of ancient dreams of world? Not think so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T04:17:59-07:00","id":228973,"title":"","content":"Then again, you freely admit that your Werewolf-fu isn't high <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T07:28:30-07:00","id":229038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228817-dreaming-uratha?p=228858#post228858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;My <b>Werewolf</b>-fu isn't high, but I couldn't remeber any thing about &quot;holy dreams&quot;. &quot;<br /> <br /> The Cahalith auspice ability?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be my first guess, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T08:16:04-07:00","id":229061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of the Moon p206, &quot;Forsaken Dreams&quot; sidebar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dreams of the Uratha are not so different from those of their mortal kin, though they tend to be simpler, tinged with an animal instinct that commands even the dreaming mind to run free, to hunt, to mate and to kill. A Forsaken\u2019s dreams are intense, emotional and always present in the moment (even when dreaming of the past or future). Generally speaking, the dreams of werewolves lack the subtlety of human dreams, with less interest in metaphor than in raw reality. When metaphor does intrude into an Uratha\u2019s dreams, it is often the raw metaphor of nature: rain cleanses and redeems, blood represents death and birth, and a cave can be shelter or the embrace of the Mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:23:14-07:00","id":229271,"title":"","content":"To me it sounds vaguely like an invitation to conflate the Shadow with whatever the Dreaming Earth is. Like &quot;these things are kinda similar conceptually and if you want they can be the same thing&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1370-ormag\u00f6den","name":"Ormag\u00f6den","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T11:45:12-07:00","id":229323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ormag\u00f6den</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/228817-dreaming-uratha?p=229271#post229271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it sounds vaguely like an invitation to conflate the Shadow with whatever the Dreaming Earth is. Like &quot;these things are kinda similar conceptually and if you want they can be the same thing&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is this sidebar on this topic in <b>Astral Realms</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dreams and Shadow</b><br /> Mages aren\u2019t sure about the relationship between the Anima Mundi and the Shadow. The Shadow is a closer mirror of the material realm \u2014 almost a different \u201cfrequency\u201d of a common reality. Shadow and Matter are tightly interwoven; one realm usually affects the other in a rapid and unambiguous fashion. (At is seems unambiguous for those versed in the lore of the Shadow Realm.) <br /> <br /> The Anima Mundi is a realm of ideal forms and essences. Human pollution from the Swath and the Spire Perilous represents mortal contributions to something eternal, or nearly so, instead of the world\u2019s day-to-day vicissitudes. As a consequence, it\u2019s often hard to map how an event in the material realm might affect the Anima Mundi or vice versa. Some cases document straightforward correspondences, but in others, events in the material realm have either taken decades to manifest astrally or haven\u2019t had any measurable effect at all.<br /> <br /> Is there a causal relationship between the two realms? Mages often believe that the Anima Mundi provides the basic template for <br /> matter and Shadow. Some Libertine scholars liken the Anima Mundi to Rupert Sheldrake\u2019s theories on morphic fields. It\u2019s a fringe element of Sleeper science, but it meshes well with the supernatural world\u2019s sympathetic laws. On the other hand, the opposite could be true: Shadow and matter interact, \u201cteaching\u201d the astral medium which form to take over time. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T13:31:02-07:00","id":229510,"title":"","content":"I've always approached the Anima Mundi from the same perspective of the rest of the Astral: it's a collective soul, consciousness, opinion, and imaginations of every single thing on Earth. Like the Tenemos, but for <i>everything</i>: each animal, plant, and element at the very least. In one part, it's the dreams of each blade of grass, but its other aspect is being the &quot;cultural&quot; perceptions and beliefs and interpretations <i>everything</i> has regarding, say, rain.<br /> <br /> So, while the Shadow develops based on what thing are and what they do (the resonances of actions and feelings accumulating), the Astral develops from beliefs and dreams.<br /> It some places, in my setting at least, they are similar enough that beings can pass between the Shadow and the Dreaming Earth. Likewise, Cahalith prophetic dreams, vision quests with altered states of consciousness, and occasionally the intense dream (ones a werewolf would believe are dreams about hunting in the Shadow or possibly Pangaea), I ST as taking place in the Astral. Also, I present a legend that all of the Incarnae that lived in the time of Pangaea were united in body, flesh, and mind; they were not sundered like the rest of the world was, and now they can move freely between the fractured realms - this is the reason the Firstborn are so elusive.<br /> <br /> Note: ruling these things like that doesn't have a major impact on my game. There aren't any mage PCs, so apart from it being &quot;shadow-like, but not the spirit world&quot;, there's not much profound knowledge there; it's just how I think of things to have some kind of consistent cosmology in the underpinnings of my game. I do like to play around with crossover stuff like that, but it gets presented from the narrow view of werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T17:32:52-07:00","id":229761,"title":"","content":"Also worth pointing out about correlations between the Astral and the Shadow: both have a boundary specifically between the &quot;places&quot; where groups of people are and the rest of their continua - the Omphalos doesn't really have &quot;thicknesses,&quot; but existing between the collective soul of humanity and the soul of the rest of the world would seem to put it in a loosely similar headspace to the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are born of exile. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}